        "stop_reason": {
          "kind": "finished",
          "message": "Implemented a complete INI parser/printer in MoonBit for the repo's dialect.\n\n## What was built\n\nThe root `ini` package is implemented by six new files (all well under the 1000-line limit), organised as a pipeline:\n\n| File | Role |\n| --- | --- |\n| `error.mbt` | `IniError` suberror + `line <n>: <reason>` message builder |\n| `scanner.mbt` | whitespace/comment/separator classes, line splitting (LF & CRLF), trimming, trailing-backslash counting, key control-character check |\n| `section_parser.mbt` | `[name]` headers: bracket matching (rejects `[[nested]]`, tails), name trimming, one-pair quote stripping, empty-name rejection |\n| `value_parser.mbt` | quoted carriers (`\"...\"`, `'...'`) with per-carrier escape tables, unquoted values with whitespace-preceded inline comments, backslash continuations |\n| `parser.mbt` | `pub fn parse`: single-pass line loop, global map vs. re-openable sections, last-wins duplicates |\n| `printer.mbt` | `pub fn print`: canonical double-quoted values, globals first, sorted entries, quote-wrapped section names when needed |\n\n`pkg.generated.mbti` was regenerated and exposes exactly `parse(StringView) -> Doc raise` and `print(Doc) -> String`.\n\n## Verification (commands actually run)\n\n- `moon test` → **51/51 pass** (the 12 public cases, including both property tests, plus 39 of mine).\n- `moon check` → 0 errors. The only two warnings come from a protected file (`test_unqualified_package` at `ini_pub_test.mbt:130`) and a false-positive `unused_package` for `moonbitlang/core/test` — I verified that removing that import breaks the build (`@test` is used by the public test), so it must stay. No warnings originate in the new code.\n- `moon fmt` and `moon fmt --check` → clean; `moon info` → interface regenerated.\n\nAdded tests (all derived from `specs/ini.md`, none hard-coded to fixtures):\n- `ini_edge_test.mbt` — line endings, comments, sections (incl. quoted/reopened names), separators, duplicate/case-sensitive keys, all three escape tables, the continuation run-length table, the continuation-line-is-text rule, and the full rejection matrix.\n- `ini_fuzz_test.mbt` — exhaustive 3,616-input sweep over the alphabet of grammar-significant characters: `parse` never traps, and every accepted document prints back to itself; plus an all-or-nothing rejection check.\n- `ini_realworld_test.mbt` — `.git/config`, a systemd unit, a `php.ini` excerpt, and Windows paths with continuations.\n- `ini_readme_example_test.mbt` — the README examples, compiled so the docs can't drift.\n\n## Notes / decisions worth knowing\n\n- **Dangling continuation:** a line break *terminates* a line, so `key=value\\` at end of input (even with a trailing newline, which is how every fixture in this repo is written) is rejected, while a marker followed by a real blank line is joined. This is the reading of \"a marker with no line after it has nothing to join to\" and it is now covered by tests both ways.\n- Continuation is decided on the raw line before escapes; joins are direct and keep the whitespace in front of the marker and the indentation of continuation lines; continuation lines contribute text, not syntax.\n- Quotes are special only when they open the value (spec's grammar: `unquoted := { any }*`), an inline comment needs preceding whitespace, and only `\"...\"` disables inline-comment handling.\n- `moon fmt` (which the task requires) also reformatted the given files `ini_spec.mbt` (`derive(...)` → `#derive(...)`) and `ini_qc.mbt` (`Int` → `Int32`); these are text-only, semantics-preserving changes made by the formatter, not by hand — `specs/`, `ini_pub_test.mbt` content and `moon.pkg` are unchanged.\n- README.md documents overview, architecture, algorithms (escape/continuation tables), usage, testing and design rationale; `README.mbt.md` (the module readme) now points at it."
        }
